    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d624">

                <pb facs="0688" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115N27/13a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-02T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1915, 8 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1770. The evidence thus far furnished indicates that <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Nebraskan</hi> was struck by a torpedo on evening of May 25.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d624-f1"/> Please inquire whether the German Government has any
                    report of attack on this vessel. It was an American vessel leaving
                    Liverpool.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d624-f1" n="1" xml:id="d624-f1-content">
                <p>The full text of depositions and reports forwarded by the Ambassador in Great
                    Britain May 28 and June 2, is printed in <hi rendition="#italic">Diplomatic
                        Correspondence with Belligerent Governments relating to Neutral Rights and
                        Duties</hi>, Department of State, European War No. 4, May 18, 1918, pp.
                    229–34; reprinted in the <hi rendition="#italic">American Journal of
                        International Law</hi>, vol. 11, Special Supplement, pp. 82–89.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
